@startuml feature-implementation-workflow
title New Feature — Implementation Workflow (team-lead delivery chain)

start

:Human\nSubmits a feature request;

:team-lead\nClassifies the request;
if (Substantive change?) then (no)
  :team-lead\nAnswers directly or makes the isolated edit;
  stop
endif

if (First substantive request this session?) then (yes)
  :team-lead\nTriggers the session-start audit;
  :template-maintainer\nPulls the latest upstream template state and\nreports what changed (proposal mode — read-only,\nat most once per session);
endif

:team-lead\nDelegates to system-analyst;

repeat
  :system-analyst\nInspects the codebase (CLAUDE.md, README, modules, DTOs,\ntests, CHANGELOG, git history)\nChecks conflicts against architecture and project conventions\nApplies scope guard (Required / Related / Optional / Out of scope);
  if (Blocking questions?) then (yes)
    :system-analyst\nRaises blocking questions;
    :team-lead\nRelays the question to the user;
    :Human\nAnswers the question;
  endif
repeat while (Questions still open?) is (yes) not (no)
:system-analyst\nReturns a plan (approach, scope, steps, impact,\nvalidation, delivery chain, Definition of Done);

:team-lead\nRelays the plan to the user;

repeat
  :Human\nReviews the plan;
repeat while (Plan approved?) is (no) not (yes)

:team-lead\nAssembles the delivery chain from the plan's Recommended Delivery Chain;

repeat
  :coder\nImplements (modules, entities, DTOs, migrations, tests);
  note right
    PostToolUse hook auto-lints every .ts on save.
    PreToolUse hook requires confirmation before
    hand-editing src/migrations/*.ts.
  end note
  :code-reviewer\nReviews (architecture, contracts, plan conformance,\ndocs freshness, test coverage);
  if (Violations found?) then (no)
    :qa-runner\nBoots the app against a real Docker-based\nPostgres/Redis stack (docker-compose.test.yml)\nand verifies it actually runs;
    note right
      Fixes environment-wiring issues itself.
      Reports genuine app bugs back to team-lead,
      which routes them back to coder.
    end note
  endif
repeat while (Violations or runtime issues found?) is (yes) not (no)

if (Established a reusable template convention?) then (yes)
  :team-lead\nInvokes template-maintainer to curate it;
  :template-maintainer\nFiles a GitHub issue suggesting the template update\n(no file written, no branch, no PR — a human decides);
endif

repeat
  :Human\nReviews the change;
repeat while (Approved to commit and push?) is (no) not (yes)

if (Change is significant?) then (yes)
  :team-lead\nAdds a dated, branch-tagged CHANGELOG.md entry;
endif

:repo-publisher\nCommits, pushes, and opens a pull request;
note right
  PreToolUse hook blocks git push --force and
  git commit --amend outright.
  PreToolUse hook runs build + test before any
  git push and denies the push on failure.
end note

:Human\nReviews and merges the PR;

stop

@enduml
